{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3263","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3263","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3263\",\"parent_revision\":\"f081c261aca03fe06a4b9bb18a39f1279934c8edcec6baf7b151a6d747766d63\",\"root_revision\":\"f081c261aca03fe06a4b9bb18a39f1279934c8edcec6baf7b151a6d747766d63\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n## Story\\n\\nAs an agent executing the `dh:swarm-task-planner` prompt, I want every phase of its documented \\\"Working Process\\\" to actually contain instructions, so that I don't have to invent behavior for an undocumented phase.\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nUnder `## Working Process` in `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md`, `### Phase 2: Dependency Analysis` contains only the literal placeholder text `[unchanged]` \u2014 no actual dependency-analysis instructions. Phase 1, 3, 4, and 5 all have real content or an explicit \\\"(UPDATED)\\\"/\\\"in addition to existing requirements\\\" delta; Phase 2 has neither.\\n\\nChecked `git log --follow -p --all -- plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md`: this exact placeholder text has existed since the file's earliest commit in this repo. There is no earlier version with real Phase 2 content to recover, and no sibling agent file or shared template defines a \\\"Phase 2: Dependency Analysis\\\" section this file could have been diffing against. The word \\\"unchanged\\\" appears to refer to a baseline that was never actually present in this repository.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\nAn agent given this prompt has zero instructions for its own dependency-analysis phase (identifying task dependencies, detecting cycles, sequencing waves) and must invent that behavior from context. For a planning agent whose whole job is producing a dependency-correct task plan, this is a real gap, not cosmetic.\\n\\n## Observations\\n\\n- Found while running the `evaluate-and-tighten-skills` no-op/duplication heuristics as a general sweep across `skills/` and `agents/` \u2014 not something the sweep itself could resolve, since writing correct Phase 2 content is a content/feature decision, not a pruning decision.\\n- `swarm-task-planner.md` also had several stray `(NEW)`/`(UPDATED)`/`[unchanged except ...]` diff-history tags elsewhere in the file (already stripped in the sweep's cleanup commit) \u2014 this Phase 2 placeholder is the one spot where the tag turned out to have no content behind it at all.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAn agent given this prompt has zero instructions for its own dependency-analysis phase (identifying task dependencies, detecting cycles, sequencing waves) and must invent that behavior from context. For a planning agent whose whole job is producing a dependency-correct task plan, this is a real gap, not cosmetic.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs an agent executing the `dh:swarm-task-planner` prompt, I want every phase of its documented \\\"Working Process\\\" to actually contain instructions, so that I don't have to invent behavior for an undocumented phase.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Discovered during a no-op/maintenance-note sweep of development-harness skills and agents (2026-08-28)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observations\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Found while running the `evaluate-and-tighten-skills` no-op/duplication heuristics as a general sweep across `skills/` and `agents/` \u2014 not something the sweep itself could resolve, since writing correct Phase 2 content is a content/feature decision, not a pruning decision.\\n- `swarm-task-planner.md` also had several stray `(NEW)`/`(UPDATED)`/`[unchanged except ...]` diff-history tags elsewhere in the file (already stripped in the sweep's cleanup commit) \u2014 this Phase 2 placeholder is the one spot where the tag turned out to have no content behind it at all.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"69699a9f3327c6a47b6665954f3b0507129f5eea01ade862c03ade78f4cab4be\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRP65rQ\"}"}